From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:30:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(repository): candidate B: the ephemeral file unsynced,
 on tmpfs on Linux

S0.4 candidate B (PLAN 11.3; D17): MEMMODE=ephemeral (the default) sets
synchronous=OFF on its temp file, since nothing in it outlives the
process; under WAL that drops only the checkpoint's sync, as NORMAL
never syncs a commit. On Linux the file goes to /dev/shm when it exists,
so its pages never reach a disk. A file DB is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 app/src/repository/db.odin | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/app/src/repository/db.odin b/app/src/repository/db.odin
index 257b6de..34bf806 100644
--- a/app/src/repository/db.odin
+++ b/app/src/repository/db.odin
@@ -101,6 +101,11 @@ db_open :: proc(path: string, mode := Mem_Mode.Ephemeral) {
 	exec("PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON;") // ON DELETE CASCADE and friends are off without it
 	exec("PRAGMA synchronous=NORMAL;") // safe under WAL, much faster than FULL
 	exec("PRAGMA journal_size_limit=67108864;") // 64 MiB: what a checkpoint leaves of the WAL file
+	if temp_path != "" {
+		// Nothing outlives the process, so nothing needs a sync: with WAL, NORMAL
+		// syncs only at a checkpoint, and OFF drops that too.
+		exec("PRAGMA synchronous=OFF;")
+	}
 	register_functions(db)
 	w.db = db
 }
@@ -172,8 +177,14 @@ ephemeral_path :: proc() -> string {
 	return path
 }
 
+// On Linux a tmpfs (/dev/shm) when there is one, so the file never reaches a disk.
 @(private = "file")
 ephemeral_dir :: proc() -> string {
+	when ODIN_OS == .Linux {
+		if os.is_dir("/dev/shm") {
+			return "/dev/shm"
+		}
+	}
 	dir, err := os.temp_directory(context.temp_allocator)
 	if err != nil || dir == "" {
 		return "."
